### Summary of semantics

- `-i` / `--ignore-case` folds only bytes `0x41`–`0x5A` (ASCII uppercase) to their lowercase equivalents for the **comparison** only.
- Emitted bytes are always the original line bytes, unmodified.
- Empty pattern still matches every line (since the empty folded pattern is a substring of any byte string).
- The flag is idempotent (setting it multiple times has no additional effect).
- It composes with `-H`, `-h`, `-r` without changing their behavior.
- Clustering works: `-ri`, `-ir`, `-Hi`, etc. all set `ignore_case = True`.
